{
  "manufacturer": "Siemens",
  "manufacturer_slug": "siemens",
  "model": "BACnet PTEC VAV Controller - Application 6657 (VAV 0-10 V Series Fan and 3-Stage Electric Heat)",
  "model_slug": "ptec-6657-vav-0-10v-series-fan-electric-heat",
  "short_model": "PTEC 0-10 V Series Fan VAV 6657",
  "aliases": [
    "PTEC 6657",
    "Application 6657",
    "App 6657",
    "550-492PA",
    "Siemens ECM series fan VAV",
    "variable speed series fan VAV"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Fan-powered VAV terminal unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Series fan-powered VAV boxes with a variable-speed fan driven by a 0-10 V signal and up to three electric heat stages plus baseboard radiation, on the Siemens BACnet PTEC controller 550-492PA.",
  "summary": "Application 6657 runs a series fan-powered VAV box whose fan speed is set by a 0-10 V signal (FAN AOV1), with up to three stages of electric heat and optional baseboard radiation, on a Siemens BACnet PTEC controller over BACnet MS/TP. Instead of DAY.NGT it uses an analog MODE point: 0 shutdown, 10 unoccupied, 20 demand reduction, 30 standby, 60 occupied. Fan airflow follows tables picked by BOX SIZE, and each heat stage needs a set fan airflow before it starts.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Newer than revision Bx40",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
    "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
    "Units are given in US units (°F, cfm, ft²); the guide also lists SI factory defaults.",
    "The guide covers controllers with firmware newer than revision Bx40; older firmware has separate documentation.",
    "MODE (AO 3) values: 0 = shutdown, 10 = unoccupied, 20 = electrical demand reduction, 30 = standby, 60 = occupied. DAY.NGT is not used.",
    "VAV AHU (BO 61) is not set by the application; it must be commanded from the field panel (PPCL) to say the air handler is running."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet PTEC Controller VAV 0 to 10V Series Fan and 3-Stage Electric Heat, Application 6657, Application Note",
    "doc_number": "140-1158",
    "revision_date": "2016-11-18",
    "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/ZGXr6lxf8pBzb_NlatPUDg/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Address the controller on the BACnet MS/TP trunk (manually or with auto addressing). The BMS sets the operating mode with MODE (AO 3), writes the occupied setpoints and VAV AHU (BO 61), and reads room temperature, primary airflow, fan airflow, heat stage status and the flow temperature alarm.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AO 3",
        "name": "MODE",
        "why": "Mode: 0 off, 10 unocc, 20 EDR, 30 standby, 60 occ"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 6",
        "name": "OCC CLG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 7",
        "name": "OCC HTG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 61",
        "name": "VAV AHU",
        "why": "Air handler running; written by the field panel"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 5",
        "name": "HEAT.COOL",
        "why": "Current mode: HEAT or COOL"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "ROOM TEMP",
        "why": "Space temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 35",
        "name": "AIR VOLUME",
        "why": "Measured primary airflow, cfm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 33",
        "name": "FAN FLOW",
        "why": "Series fan airflow command, cfm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 43",
        "name": "HEAT STAGE 1",
        "why": "Electric heat stage 1 on/off"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 62",
        "name": "FLOW TEMP",
        "why": "Supply air not cooling the room"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Occupancy and operating mode come from MODE (AO 3), not DAY.NGT: 0 = shutdown, 10 = unoccupied, 20 = electrical demand reduction, 30 = standby, 60 = occupied. UNOCC OVRD (BO 21) shows a temporary occupied override from the room unit button.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "VAV AHU (BO 61) must be commanded by the field panel (PPCL) to tell the box whether the central air handler is on; the application only reads it. VENT DMD MIN (AO 107) sets the occupied ventilation minimum airflow.",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP only. CTLR ADDRESS (AO 1) holds the MS/TP address; the point table lists its factory value as 255.",
      "APPLICATION (AO 2) holds the application number; the point table lists its factory default as 6699."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "With a digital room unit (revision 26 and later), a command sent through the room unit puts the matching BACnet input Out Of Service.",
      "Loop gains, motor timing, rotation angles and setup codes are commissioning values; don't write them from the BMS routinely.",
      "In shutdown mode the fan stops only after all electric heat stages have been off for 30 seconds."
    ]
  },
